Exempt the two HAP pairing endpoints from go2rtc's Basic-auth middleware

The HomeKit Accessory Protocol is served on the API port (internal/homekit
passes Port: uint16(api.Port)), but middlewareAuth has no path exemption. HAP
speaks its own protocol and cannot send HTTP Basic credentials, so an iPhone's
pairing request is answered with 401 and the Home app fails to add the
accessory. Measured on 1.9.14+dev.506cfa7: POST /pair-setup, /pair-verify and
/accessories all return 401 once api.username is set. The practical effect is
that native HomeKit and API authentication are mutually exclusive, with no
diagnostic pointing at the cause.

Only /pair-setup and /pair-verify need exempting, and neither is left
unprotected:

  - pair-setup is guarded by the setup PIN via SRP.
  - pair-verify is guarded by the long-term keys established during pairing.
  - Everything afterwards (/accessories, /characteristics, events) runs inside
    the encrypted HAP connection that pkg/hksv hijacks from the ResponseWriter,
    so it never re-enters this mux and is unaffected.

Verified against skrashevich/go2rtc @ 506cfa7d: applies cleanly and `go build
./...` is clean.

diff --git a/internal/api/api.go b/internal/api/api.go
index dfb65117..3e18410d 100644
